  "id": "COMPOUND:18448 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between the entity GKWHCQAFBYRUIH-NKVSYTJASA-N and Phosphodiesterase 6C through multiple indirect pathways. The entity is implicated in targeting SNB-78, which is a target of several compounds, including Suregadolide D and 12-O-Deacetyl-12-Epi-19-Deoxy-22-Hydroxyscalarin, both of which have a target of Phosphodiesterase 6C. Additionally, the entity is linked to JM1, which is a target of Maoesin A, which also targets Phosphodiesterase 6C. These findings collectively indicate that the entity may be involved in the regulation of Phosphodiesterase 6C through different molecular mechanisms, possibly through the activation or inhibition of downstream targets. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role in modulating phosphodiesterase activity, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
